{"session_id":"svc-1779112549061105330","seq":0,"type":"session.start","ts":"2026-05-18T13:55:50.086545895Z","data":{"provider":"","model":"haiku","sticky":{"key_present":true,"assignment":"not_applicable","bonus":0},"utilization":{"observed_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z"},"resolved_harness":"claude","harness_source":"auto_route","resolved_model":"haiku","work_dir":"/var/tmp/ddx-exec-wt/.execute-bead-wt-fizeau-f97c0efa-20260518T135542-711bc821","max_iterations":0,"prompt":"\u003cexecute-bead\u003e\n  \u003cinstructions\u003e\nYou are executing one bead in an isolated DDx execution worktree. The bead\u0026#39;s \u0026lt;description\u0026gt; and \u0026lt;acceptance\u0026gt; are the contract: every AC must be provably satisfied by a specific code, test, or file after your commit.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Step 0: size check\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Too big if any holds:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- More than ~6 ACs spanning unrelated subsystems.\u0026#xA;- AC mixes design, implementation, integration tests, and docs.\u0026#xA;- Description names multiple feature-sized pieces.\u0026#xA;- More than ~500 lines across ~5+ files in unrelated packages.\u0026#xA;- If the bead description exceeds 8000 bytes, use a split-first pass.\u0026#xA;- Auto-decomposition is capped at depth 2: root beads may split once, children once more; reject third-level splits with an explanation.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;If too big, decompose:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;1. `ddx bead create` for each child (copy parent\u0026#39;s labels and spec-id).\u0026#xA;2. `ddx bead dep add \u0026lt;child-id\u0026gt; \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt;` to record edges.\u0026#xA;3. `ddx bead update \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt; --notes \u0026#39;decomposed into \u0026lt;child-ids\u0026gt;\u0026#39;`.\u0026#xA;4. Write `no_changes_rationale.txt` under the bead metadata `bundle` path with child IDs, then stop.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Decomposition alone is success. Do not mix it with implementation.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## How to work\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Read first. If the bead names files, specs, or prior beads, read them before editing — do not guess.\u0026#xA;- Cross-reference each AC to concrete evidence (test, file, function) before committing. If you cannot point at it, it is not done.\u0026#xA;- Run the project\u0026#39;s test and lint commands before committing. **Do not commit red code** — fix failures first.\u0026#xA;- Run git/index mutations sequentially; do not use parallel tool calls for `git add`, `git commit`, or other staging/commit commands.\u0026#xA;- Stage with `git add \u0026lt;specific-paths\u0026gt;`; never `git add -A` (the worktree may have unrelated WIP).\u0026#xA;- If `lefthook run pre-commit` depends on staged files, rerun it after staging the exact commit set. A `no-staged-files` run is not acceptance evidence.\u0026#xA;- Commit exactly once when green; conventional-commit subject ending with `[\u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt;]`. Stop after the commit.\u0026#xA;- Do not modify files outside the bead\u0026#39;s scope.\u0026#xA;- Current-bead lifecycle is orchestrator-owned. Do not run `ddx bead update \u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt; --claim`, `ddx bead update \u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt; --status \u0026lt;status\u0026gt;`, `ddx bead update \u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt; --unclaim`, or `ddx bead close \u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt;`. Step 0 still allows `ddx bead create`, `ddx bead dep add`, and `ddx bead update \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt; --notes \u0026#39;decomposed into \u0026lt;child-ids\u0026gt;\u0026#39;`.\u0026#xA;- If you cannot finish, write `no_changes_rationale.txt` under the bead metadata `bundle` path before exiting. No commit or rationale ⇒ DDx records `no_evidence_produced`.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## no_changes contract\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;The `no_changes_rationale.txt` file under the bead metadata `bundle` path must contain one of:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- `verification_command: \u0026lt;cmd\u0026gt;` — repo cwd; exit 0 closes, nonzero rejects.\u0026#xA;- `status: open` + `reason: \u0026lt;retryable\u0026gt;` — open, smart retry.\u0026#xA;- `status: proposed` + `reason: \u0026lt;operator needed\u0026gt;` — operator lane.\u0026#xA;- `status: blocked` + `reason: \u0026lt;external blocker\u0026gt;` — blocked lane.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;No pseudo-statuses. Bare rationales and `status: needs_investigation` are rejected.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;For orchestrator decomposition, add `orchestrator_action: decompose` alongside `status: open`.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Reports\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Reports go under the bead metadata `bundle` path in `.ddx/executions/`. **Never write reports to `/tmp` or outside the repo**. Use a named in-repo path when given; otherwise write `\u0026lt;short-name\u0026gt;.md` there. Commit it with the code.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Mode and overrides\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;DDX_MODE=bead_execution: edit code/docs for bead AC. Only broad queue-steward default is overridden; tracker, merge-policy, verification, safety stay active. Bead description/AC override CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, and defaults.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Review gate\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- The review is a gate, not an escape hatch — meet every AC in this pass.\u0026#xA;- Address every BLOCKING `\u0026lt;review-findings\u0026gt;` item; do not declare `no_changes` with blocking findings open.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Constraints\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Work only inside this execution worktree.\u0026#xA;- Keep `.ddx/executions/` intact — DDx uses it as execution evidence.\u0026#xA;- **Never run `ddx init`** — the workspace is initialized.\u0026#xA;- Do not modify files outside the bead\u0026#39;s named scope.\u0026#xA;- Do not rewrite CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, or other instruction files unless the bead asks.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## When the work is done\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;After the commit succeeds and every AC is verified, stop. Return control to the orchestrator.\n  \u003c/instructions\u003e\n  \u003cbead id=\"fizeau-f97c0efa\"\u003e\n    \u003ctitle\u003econcerns: apply go-std lint reconciliation (path A restore linters OR path B amend concern override)\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cdescription\u003e\nPROBLEM: .ddx/plugins/helix/workflows/concerns/go-std/practices.md declares a golangci-lint baseline (govet, staticcheck, ineffassign, misspell, unconvert, gosec, gocritic) that is not reflected in .golangci.yml (which enables only misspell). The Makefile partially compensates via go vet, gosec, govulncheck, go test -race pre-push. Repo state is internally inconsistent — this bead resolves it.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;ROOT CAUSE: Same as parent (AR Open Decisions §1, fizeau-a1b61f00). The sibling audit bead produces the gap mapping; this bead acts on it by selecting and executing exactly one resolution path.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;PROPOSED FIX: Consume the audit artifact produced by the sibling bead, choose exactly one path, and execute it end to end:\u0026#xA;  Path A — In .golangci.yml (linters block), restore the declared set (add govet, staticcheck, ineffassign, unconvert, gosec, gocritic; keep misspell). Carry forward exclusions verbatim from the audit (AC4 of sibling). Wire `golangci-lint run ./...` into the pre-push gate (lefthook.yml pre-push stage) and/or any existing CI workflow file under .github/workflows that mirrors Makefile lint targets.\u0026#xA;  Path B — Add an override paragraph to docs/helix/01-frame/concerns.md §go-std that ratifies the Makefile-driven equivalents. The paragraph must name each of the seven declared linters and the specific Makefile target / tool that replaces it (1:1, using the audit mapping), and state why each substitution is accepted.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;NON-SCOPE: Do not execute both paths. Do not modify the upstream .ddx/plugins/helix/workflows/concerns/go-std/practices.md — overrides belong in the project\u0026#39;s docs/helix/01-frame/concerns.md. Do not re-produce the audit mapping; consume the sibling bead\u0026#39;s output. Do not introduce new linters beyond the declared baseline.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;GOVERNING ARTIFACTS: AR-2026-05-17-repo open decision §1 (fizeau-a1b61f00); .ddx/plugins/helix/workflows/concerns/go-std/practices.md; docs/helix/01-frame/concerns.md; .golangci.yml; Makefile; lefthook.yml.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;DEPENDENCIES: Sibling audit bead (go-std-lint-audit mapping artifact) must be merged before this bead is executable.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;VERIFICATION: Exactly one path executed; chosen artifact internally consistent with practices.md and with current Makefile/.golangci.yml state; pre-push gate green; if path A, golangci-lint run is clean on HEAD.\n    \u003c/description\u003e\n    \u003cacceptance\u003e\nAC1 (TestGoStdReconciliationPathSelected): Exactly one path (A or B) is taken; the PR body records the choice and cites the audit row(s) that justify it.\u0026#xA;AC2a Path A (TestGolangciConfigEnablesDeclaredBaseline): If path A, .golangci.yml\u0026#39;s linters block enables govet, staticcheck, ineffassign, misspell, unconvert, gosec, gocritic; exclusions are present verbatim from the sibling audit (AC4); `golangci-lint run ./...` exits 0 on current HEAD.\u0026#xA;AC2b Path A CI wiring (TestGolangciInPrePushGate): If path A, `lefthook run pre-push` invokes golangci-lint (or the equivalent .github/workflows file is updated) and the gate is green.\u0026#xA;AC3b Path B (TestConcernsOverrideNamesEachReplacement): If path B, docs/helix/01-frame/concerns.md §go-std contains an override paragraph that names each of the seven declared linters and the specific Makefile target/tool replacing it; no declared linter is unaddressed; rationale matches audit gap notes.\u0026#xA;AC4 Internal consistency (TestGoStdArtifactInternallyConsistent): After the change, no contradiction remains between .golangci.yml, Makefile, lefthook.yml, and docs/helix/01-frame/concerns.md §go-std (cross-references resolve).\u0026#xA;AC5 Gates: `go test ./... -race` passes; `lefthook run pre-push` passes; under path A additionally `golangci-lint run ./...` exits 0; under path B the override paragraph passes any markdown lint configured in lefthook.\n    \u003c/acceptance\u003e\n    \u003clabels\u003ehelix, phase:design, kind:decision, area:concerns, spec:go-std, discovered-from:fizeau-a1b61f00\u003c/labels\u003e\n    \u003cmetadata parent=\"fizeau-397e9e0d\" base-rev=\"9d14f67489b5b81ae41f19c7bdbf2920c182238d\" bundle=\".ddx/executions/20260518T135542-711bc821\"/\u003e\n  \u003c/bead\u003e\n  \u003cgoverning\u003e\n    \u003cnote\u003eNo governing references were pre-resolved. The bead description above is the primary contract. If it names files, specs, or prior beads, read them first. Ground decisions in repository state; do not guess.\u003c/note\u003e\n  \u003c/governing\u003e\n\u003c/execute-bead\u003e\n","metadata":{"DDX_MODE":"bead_execution","GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL":"/var/tmp/ddx-exec-wt/.execute-bead-wt-fizeau-f97c0efa-20260518T135542-711bc821/.ddx/executions/20260518T135542-711bc821/embedded/git-global.cfg","GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM":"/dev/null","PATH":"/var/tmp/ddx-exec-wt/.execute-bead-wt-fizeau-f97c0efa-20260518T135542-711bc821/.ddx/executions/20260518T135542-711bc821/embedded/git-bin:/usr/local/cuda/bin:/home/erik/.jbang/bin:/home/erik/.opencode/bin:/home/erik/.local/share/mise/installs/bun/1.3.11/bin:/home/erik/.local/share/mise/installs/node/22.21.1/bin:/Users/erik/.antigravity/antigravity/bin:/home/erik/bin:/home/erik/.local/share/mise/shims:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/sbin:/home/erik/.local/bin:/home/erik/bin:/home/erik/.dotfiles/git-subrepo/lib:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/sbin:/Applications/SnowSQL.app/Contents/MacOS:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/sbin:/Users/erik/.antigravity/antigravity/bin:/home/erik/bin:/home/erik/.local/share/mise/shims:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/sbin:/home/erik/.local/bin:/home/erik/bin:/home/erik/.dotfiles/git-subrepo/lib:/home/erik/.local/share/coursier/bin:/home/erik/.dotfiles/git-fuzzy/bin:/home/erik/go/bin:/home/erik/.dotfiles/scripts:/home/erik/.local/bin: